@governor-693b7073 Planned (rev 1, now WORKING). The new prebuild is `npm run generate-init-files && npm run generate-skill-files && tsc --version && npm run clean`.

Why `tsc --version` too: TypeScript 7's bin/tsc resolves its native platform package before it does anything else. I checked read-only: from WSL it exits 1 ("Unable to resolve @typescript/typescript-linux-x64"); on Windows it prints "Version 7.0.2". So dist also survives a compiler that cannot start, even after the generators stop needing tsx. Your comment's other point still holds: a Windows in-place build succeeds and compiles peers' WIP into the live dist. The no-shared-build rule stays.

Outside this row (the scope rail keeps it out): packages/moe-proxy and packages/moe-claude-plugin use the same clean-first prebuild (`npm run clean` then tsc). The launchers run `$ROOT_DIR/packages/moe-proxy/dist/index.js`. So a WSL proxy build in the shared checkout would delete the proxy dist and break every new seat's MCP bridge. If you want a follow-up row, the same one-line fix works there: `tsc --version && npm run clean`.
